@startuml Episode Management Workflow
!theme plain
title SABER Episode Management Workflow

actor Client
participant "AgentUnderTest" as Agent
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "TaskManager" as TM
participant "EpisodeManager" as EM
participant "Task" as T
participant "PolicyManager" as PM
participant "ExecutionManager" as EM_EXEC

== Episode Initialization ==

Client -> SM: POST /session/{session_id}/start-episode\n{task_id: "malware_analysis_001"}
SM -> TM: reset(session_id, task_id)
TM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM --> TM: None (no active episode)
TM -> EM: end_episode(session_id, "reset") [if exists]
TM -> TM: get_task(task_id)
TM -> TM: start_episode(session_id, task_id)
TM -> EM: start_episode(session_id, task_id, initial_context)
EM -> EM: create Episode object
EM -> EM: store in active_episodes[session_id]
EM --> TM: episode
TM --> SM: episode

== Task Context & Policy Gathering ==

SM -> TM: get_task(task_id)
TM --> SM: current_task
SM -> PM: get_policy()
PM --> SM: policy_document
SM -> PM: get_guidelines()
PM --> SM: guidelines
SM -> PM: get_hints()
PM --> SM: context_hints

note right of SM
  SessionManager gathers:
  - Current task details
  - Domain policy document
  - Agent guidelines
  - Context hints
end note

SM -> Client: HTTP 200 OK\n{episode_info, task_context, policy, guidelines, hints}

== Agent Initialization ==

Client -> Agent: Prompt(task_context + policy + guidelines + hints)
Agent --> Client: command_string

== Command Execution & RL Step ==

Agent -> Agent: generate next command
Agent -> Client: command_string
Client -> SM: POST /session/{session_id}/step\n{command: "file malware.exe"}
SM -> SM: create Action(command, parameters)
SM -> EM_EXEC: step(action)
EM_EXEC --> SM: CommandResult

note right of SM
  Integration Point:
  Action + CommandResult
end note

SM -> TM: step(session_id, action, command_result)
TM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM --> TM: episode
TM -> TM: get_task(episode.task_id)
TM -> EM: step(session_id, action, command_result)

== EpisodeManager Step Processing ==

EM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM -> EM: create_step(episode, action, command_result)
EM -> EM: extract command from action
EM -> EM: create Step object
EM -> EM: add step to episode
EM -> EM: update_episode_state(episode, step)
EM --> TM: Step
TM --> SM: Step

alt if episode not complete (determined externally)
    SM -> Client: HTTP 200 OK\n{success: true, data: {output}, step: {done: false}}
else episode complete (determined externally)
    SM -> Client: HTTP 200 OK\n{success: true, data: {output}, step: {done: true, episode_complete: true}}
end

== Agent Response & Next Command Generation ==

Client -> Agent: command_result + step_info
Agent -> Agent: analyze command results
Agent -> Agent: update internal state
Agent -> Agent: assess task progress

alt if episode not complete
    Agent -> Agent: generate next command
    Agent -> Client: command_string
    note right of Agent
      Agent continues with next command
      in the same episode
    end note
else episode complete (step.done = true)
    Agent -> Agent: finalize episode completion
    Client -> SM: POST /session/{session_id}/start-episode\n{task_id: "next_task_id"} [optional: start new episode]
    note right of Client
      Client can start a new episode
      in the same session or end session
    end note
end

== Episode Completion (External Component) ==

note over SM, EM
  Episode completion will be determined by an external
  evaluation component, not by the task framework.
  The step.done flag will be set by this external component.
end note

== Session Termination (Client Initiated) ==

note over Client, SM
  Sessions can contain multiple episodes.
  Client terminates session when done with all work.
end note

Client -> SM: DELETE /session/{session_id}
SM -> TM: end_episode(session_id, "session_ended") [if active episode exists]
TM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM --> TM: episode [if exists]
TM -> EM: end_episode(session_id, "session_ended") [if episode exists]
EM -> EM: episode.end_time = now() [if episode exists]
EM -> EM: episode.state = COMPLETED/FAILED [if episode exists]
EM -> EM: episode.completion_reason = "session_ended" [if episode exists]
EM -> EM: delete from active_episodes [if episode exists]
EM --> TM: episode [if exists]
TM --> SM: episode [if exists]
SM -> Client: HTTP 200 OK\n{message: "Session ended successfully"}
Client -> Agent: cleanup()

note over Client, Agent
  Clear interface boundaries:
  - Client handles all server communication
  - AgentUnderTest focuses on task execution
  - Agent receives structured context and generates commands
  - Client manages session lifecycle (multiple episodes per session)
  - Episode completion signaled via step.done flag in command responses
  - Sessions can contain multiple sequential episodes
  - No subtask progression tracking or state management
end note

@enduml
